    <description><![CDATA[<p><b>Time fetched:</b> 5:19PM EDT<br/><b>Next update:</b> 11:19PM EDT</p><h2>GREAT LAKES SURFACE WATER TEMPERATURE</h2><p><b>Status:</b> CURRENT DAILY (satellite composite)</p><p><b>Legend</b><br><img src="https://wyattleathorn7.github.io/great-lakes-live-environment/water_temperature/legend.png?v=glsea-Sun-27-Sep-2026-06-51-11-GMT" width="600" alt="legend"><br>Surface water temperature (°F): cold <b>53°F</b> (deep blue) → <b>61.5°F</b> → warm <b>70°F</b> (red). Lakewide mean this run: <b>62.1°F</b>.</p><p><b>Source:</b> NOAA/GLERL CoastWatch GLSEA (Great Lakes Surface Environmental Analysis)<br/><a href="https://apps.glerl.noaa.gov/coastwatch/webdata/glsea/cur/glsea_cur.asc">https://apps.glerl.noaa.gov/coastwatch/webdata/glsea/cur/glsea_cur.asc</a></p><p>Transparent outside valid water data so existing project layers (shipwrecks, lighthouses, harbors, parks) stay visible. Turn on/off independently of wave and ice layers.</p><p><i>Not endorsed by NOAA.</i></p>]]></description>
